@startuml overview_state
title bridgeIQ — App Overview: how the two main flows are entered

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor #FDFDFD
  BorderColor #444
  ArrowColor #444
}

[*] --> Idle : app launch (opening screen)

state Idle {
  Idle : Pre-deal configuration (Config menu)
  Idle : • Player type per seat — HUMAN / COMPUTER / NETWORK   (player_config)
  Idle : • Bidding system per seat — SAYC / 2-1 / Acol / French / Precision
  Idle : • Bidding engine — native_bidder | BEN     • Card engine — no-peek | MC | DD
}

state "WHOLE GAME\n(deal -> bid -> play -> score)" as WholeGame #E8F4FF
state "CARD-PLAY ONLY\n(contract set -> play -> score)" as CardPlay #FFF3E0

Idle --> WholeGame : First Deal / Next Deal\n_on_new_deal() : phase='bidding'
Idle --> CardPlay  : MiniBridge mode\n_maybe_run_minibridge_rounds() : set_contract_direct()
Idle --> CardPlay  : Repeat Deal — "keep contract,\nskip auction"  : set_contract_direct(preserved)

WholeGame --> Idle : Next Deal / quit
CardPlay  --> Idle : Next Deal / quit

note right of WholeGame
  Variations (same phase machine):
  • Local AI table (all COMPUTER)
  • Human South vs AI (default)
  • One-player hand entry
  • Network biq<->biq (NETWORK seats)
  • A/B-off vs whole-system test run
  See 01/02 diagrams.
end note

note right of CardPlay
  Variations:
  • MiniBridge (points + contract dialogs)
  • Repeat Deal keeping prior contract
  See 03/04 diagrams.
end note
@enduml
